	"Mon.8": "PLACEHOLDER",
	"Mon.9": "PLACEHOLDER",
	"Mon.10": "PLACEHOLDER",
	
	"Tue.1": "It's a beautiful day, isn't it?#$e#I wish I had less work to do.$s",
	"Tue.2": "If you ever have questions and I'm not available, ask Maru.#$b#She's very knowledgeable.$h",
	"Tue.3": "There's a documentary about the medical practices of ancient civilizations on TV later tonight.#$b#Hopefully I'll finish my reports in time for it.$s",
	"Tue.4": "I have to do a lot of reading to keep up with the best practices for patient care.#$e#At least I like reading!$h",
	"Tue.5": "I want to form a good rapport with my patients, but getting too close presents a conflict of interest.$s#$b#It's a difficult balance to maintain.#$e#We can be friendly, but we can't entirely be friends.",
	"Tue.6": "Did you know you can develop allergies later in life?#$b#It happens very commonly with shellfish, actually.",
	"Tue.7": "It's difficult knowing that no matter how much advice I give, it's up to my patients whether or not they take it.#$e#There are some people in this town I worry about quite a lot.$s",
	"Tue.8": "Don't overwork yourself, @. #$e#If our farmers get sick, where will we get our food? We need you!$h",
	"Tue.9": "It's good to see you, @.$h#$e#I admit it's nice to have something to get out of bed for besides work.$l",
	"Tue.10": "They say that just smiling more can improve your health.#$e#I was always a little dubious about that.#$b#Being with you is starting to convince me, though.$h",

	"Wed.1": "Remember to cover your mouth when you sneeze.#$e#Then make sure to wash your hands.",
	"Wed.2": "It's a great help having Maru working at the clinic.#$e#She invented an entirely new way of organizing our records. It's much more intuitive!$h",
	"Wed.3": "I moved here right after graduating my residency.#$e#That would have been... wow. Longer ago than I thought.$s",
	"Wed.4": "I swear I do leave the clinic sometimes.#$b#I'm often at the museum on Saturdays, if you're ever on that side of town.$h",
	"Wed.5": "I've found that it's good for my health to try and stay positive.#$e#It's not always easy, but I do think you can find a silver lining on any cloud if you look hard enough.",
	"Wed.6": "It's nice to have another friend in town.$h#$e# I always worried that I was boring Maru when it was just the two of us.",
	"Wed.7": "You know, I had a lot of acquaintances during my time in medical school...#$b#I don't know if I ever had any actual friends.$s",
	"Wed.8": "It's funny. In an emergency situation I almost forget to be afraid: all that matters is taking care of the patient.#$e$It usually only catches up to me afterwards.$s#$b#That's probably better than the alternative.",
	"Wed.9": "You have a really healthy glow. That's good.$h",
	"Wed.10": "Usually by the middle of the week I'd be starting to hit a slump.#$b#I think your energy is infectious!$h",
	
	"Thu.1": "I live above the clinic. I admit it's convenient, not having a commute.",
	"Thu.2": "Nutrition is important, so make sure and eat well. #$b#$q TH2Pos/TH2Neg TH2None#Home-cooked meals are best. Do you cook?#$r TH2Pos 25 TH2Yes#I love to cook!#$r TH2Pos 0 TH2Busy#I'm usually too busy...#$r TH2Neg -5 TH2No#I have more important things to spend time on.",
	"Thu.3": "I'm what you'd call a family practice physician.#$e#Taking care of someone from birth to death... that's a lot of responsibility. I take it very seriously.",
	"Thu.4": "I probably drink more coffee than is strictly healthy.$s#$e#But all that paperwork wouldn't get done otherwise!",
	"Thu.5": "I try and attend every town festival, even if I find crowds overwhelming.#$e#It's good for me to get out of the clinic sometimes.",
	"Thu.6": "%revealtaste:Maru:432 I tried making my own pickles once.#$b#I think I'm the reason Maru won't eat them now.$s",
	"Thu.7": "Do you ever listen to music while you're working?#$b#I find it helps the time go by much more quickly.$h",
	"Thu.8": "I always wanted to work in a smaller, underserved community.#$b#It can vastly improve quality of life to have easier access to medical care.#$e#Imagine how much crankier George would be if he had to go all the way to Zuzu City for his checkups!$h",
	"Thu.9": "I wrote the wrong date on a report the other day.#$e#I was thinking about you and got distracted.$l",
	"Thu.10": "Maintaining work-life balance has always been something I struggle with.$s#$e#If I didn't live alone I think it would be easier.$l",

	"Fri.1": "Feel free to stop by my office if you're ever feeling ill.#$e#Though the farming lifestyle is very active. You'll probably stay healthy without trying.$h",
	"Fri.2": "Remember to stay hydrated. You'd be surprised at how many people don't drink enough water.",
	"Fri.3": "Any exciting plans for the weekend, @?#$e#Remember, everything in moderation!",
	"Fri.4": "You're welcome to visit me at my apartment any time you like.#$e#I don't often have company. It would be a nice change of pace.",
	"Fri.5": "I've found that being a doctor is very fulfilling work.#$e#I've always felt happiest when I'm helping other people.",
	"Fri.6": "It's kind of you to make time to talk with me, @.#$b#It always brightens my day.$h",
	"Fri.7": "Living where I work makes some things easier... on the other hand, it makes it difficult to ever stop working.",
	"Fri.8": "I had a phase as a child where I was convinced I wanted to be a jazz pianist.#$b#At my first recital I threw up before I even got on stage. I never played the piano again.#$e#It was mortifying then but it's kind of funny now.$h",
	"Fri.9": "I've been thinking about setting up a little herb garden in my window.#$e#If you have any tips for keeping plants alive, I'd love to hear them.$h",
	"Fri.10": "@, I know I'm not technically your doctor...#$b#But if you ever need a 'confidential checkup' you know where to find me.$l",

	"Sat.1": "I never really relax, even on weekends.#$e#It's not as though I can say 'sorry, it's my day off' if there's a medical emergency.",
	"Sat.2": "Did you know the museum library has an extensive microfiche collection?#$e# It's fascinating to read news articles from decades ago. Things were very different then.",
	"Sat.3": "I imagine even on weekends the farm requires a lot of attention.#$e#Ha... you and I both have jobs that it's hard to ever really put down.",
	"Sat.4": "Are you sleeping enough,@?#$e#At the very least you should be going to bed before midnight.",
	"Sat.5": "I like that Pelican town is small enough that you can walk everywhere.#$e#Driving always made me a little nervous.",
	"Sat.6": "Another week is almost over... it feels like the older I get, the faster they fly by.$s",
	"Sat.7": "I came here because I liked the small-town atmosphere and the potential for a truly holistic approach to patient care.#$e#I've grown to really love it.$h",
	"Sat.8": "Maybe I'll actually take it easy this weekend.#$e#I could finally open that bottle of wine I've been saving.",
	"Sat.9": "%Harvey is humming an upbeat jazz tune and seems completely distracted.",
	"Sat.10": "*Sigh*... I'm starting to feel kind of old...#$e#The older you get the more memories you're burdened with. It can be overwhelming.$s#$e#I think I'll stay younger with you around.$h",

	"Sun.1": "It's always difficult to fully enjoy Sundays, knowing that Monday is just around the corner.",
	"Sun.2": "Hmm... I'm struggling to make ends meet. I don't have enough patients.#$e#I suppose that's the trade-off for working in a rural community.",
	"Sun.3": "Be careful if you're going to go down into the mines.#$e#Remember to wear closed-toed shoes!",
	"Sun.4": "As a doctor, I'm well aware of the benefits of home-cooked food. But I'm so busy, I have a hard time bringing myself to cook.",
	"Sun.5": "I'd strongly recommend against drinking Joja Cola.#$e#I've read the ingredient list and it's... concerning.$s",
	"Sun.6": "My colleagues in Zuzu City keep telling me I should move there if money's so tight out here.#$e#I tried city life during medical school and I can say with confidence that it's not for me. Far too fast-paced.",
	"Sun.7": "Medical school was difficult, but I've never regretted the decision to pursue it.#$b#It's more than a career for me; it's a vocation. It gives me purpose.",
	"Sun.8": "Imagine having a patient's life completely in your hands, and failing to keep them alive... that's something that will haunt you forever.$s#$e#Hypothetically.",
	"Sun.9": "Some people know what they want to do with their lives from a very young age. I envy that.#$e#It took me a lot of false starts to get to where I am and I've always felt a little behind because of it.",
	"Sun.10": "Do you ever get lonely living by yourself on the farm, @?#$e#Just wondering.$l",

	"Spring.Weekly.0.1": "It's officially pollen season.#$b#Living in the countryside seems like it would be a little less idyllic for a person with bad allergies.",
	"Spring.Weekly.0.2": "%revealtaste:Harvey:22 Did you know that dandelion greens are edible?#$b#Most people consider them weeds, but they're not bad in a salad.",
	"Spring.Weekly.0.3": "If there's something that you need from the clinic, I'd advise stopping by earlier in the day.",
	"Spring.Weekly.0.4": "Be sure to cook any fish you catch thoroughly before you eat it.",

	"Spring.Weekly.2.1": "Hi, @. Are you having a productive Spring so far?#$e#Remember not to give yourself more work than you can comfortably handle.",
	"Spring.Weekly.2.2": "It's Spring cleaning season again. It must take a lot of work to keep %farm Farm tidy.",
	"Spring.Weekly.2.3": "Remember to eat a healthy breakfast before you start in on your farm chores.#$e#It's the most important meal of the day, as they say.",
	"Spring.Weekly.2.4": "Maru works at the clinic on Tuesdays and Thursdays.#$e#She's been a huge help since she started.",

	"Spring.Weekly.4.1": "%revealtaste:Harvey:18 My favorite flower is the daffodil.#$e#They're not particularly exciting, but they're bright and cheerful, and they come back reliably every year.$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.4.2": "%revealtaste:Harvey:399 Patches of spring onions grow down past Marnie's barn, across the river.#$e#I'd go pick some myself if my schedule wasn't so tight.",
	"Spring.Weekly.4.3": "I really need to put aside time to clear out the magazines in the clinic waiting room...#$e#There are definitely some in there old enough to qualify as historical documents.",
	"Spring.Weekly.4.4": "Spring means the days are getting longer again.#$e#And yet I still feel like I never have enough time to get everything done.",

	"Spring.Weekly.6.1": "Sometimes I feel as though I put so much energy into taking care of my patients that I don't have any left over to take care of myself...$s#$e#...Ah! I'm fine though, really!$8",
	"Spring.Weekly.6.2": "%revealtaste:Maru:400 Spring is strawberry season.#$b#It's all Maru talks about this time of year. They're her favorite.",
	"Spring.Weekly.6.3": "I've thought about getting a pet to keep me company.#$e#My apartment barely has enough room in it for me, though, let alone a cat or a dog.#$b#I'd feel bad keeping one cooped up in there.$s",
	"Spring.Weekly.6.4": "I've been reading a book about historical agricultural practices. It's just fascinating!$h#$b#You're welcome to borrow it when I'm done, if you want.",

	"Spring.Weekly.8.1": "There's a bird's nest in the tree outside my clinic. If you look closely you can see the eggs!$h#$b#Not too closely, though, or mama bird will get mad.",
	"Spring.Weekly.8.2": "Would you like to join me on my afternoon walks sometimes, @?#$e#Walking is an easy way to stay active, but it's more fun with company!$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.8.3": "Have you planted any flowers this Spring, @?#$e#I wish I had the space for a flower garden.#$b#I'm a little jealous of you!$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.8.4": "I never have to worry about setting my alarm clock in Spring.#$b#The birds outside my window are always loud enough to wake me up before it goes off.$h",

	"Spring.Weekly.10.1": "The flowers look brighter this year, somehow.#$e#Or maybe I'm just noticing them more.$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.10.2": "There's always an upswing in air-traffic this time of year.#$e#It's not surprising that people enjoy flying more when it's nice out.",
	"Spring.Weekly.10.3": "It's been so pleasant outside since the season turned... we should plan a picnic!$h",
	"Spring.Weekly.10.4": "Spending time with you always puts a Spring in my step.$l#$e#Haha. Too much?$h", 

	"Summer.Weekly.0.1": "Be careful running around in the tall grass! Watch out for bees.",
	"Summer.Weekly.0.2": "It feels like a shame that I spend so much of Summer indoors...$s#$e#Oh, well. It can't be helped.",
	"Summer.Weekly.0.3": "If you're planning to stay out in the sun for extended periods of time, I'd recommend a hat.",
	"Summer.Weekly.0.4": "When applying sunscreen, don't forget to put some behind your ears.",

	"Summer.Weekly.2.1": "Sometimes there's broken glass in the sand at the beach.#$e#Be careful where you step if you walk around near the water without shoes on.",
	"Summer.Weekly.2.2": "Remember to drink plenty of water and give yourself regular breaks.#$e#I know you have a lot to do on the farm, but heat stroke is no joke!",
	"Summer.Weekly.2.3": "If you're looking for something to do with your time, it's always worth it to check the bulletin board outside of Pierre's shop.",
	"Summer.Weekly.2.4": "If you often find yourself a target for mosquitos, you're more likely to have Type O blood.#$e#At least, anecdotal evidence suggests that's the flavor they like best.",

	"Summer.Weekly.4.1": "You can see a lot of unique wildlife down at the tidepools by the beach.#$e#Be careful of the urchins! Some of them are venomous, and none of them like to be stepped on.",
	"Summer.Weekly.4.2": "It probably seems silly to drink hot coffee when the weather is like this.#$e#I'm a creature of habit, I suppose.",
	"Summer.Weekly.4.3": "If you have a moment, can you help me with something?#$b#Oh, it's nothing serious, don't worry!$h#$b#$q SW43Pollywogs/SW43Tadpoles SW43None#Do you call baby frogs 'pollywogs' or 'tadpoles'? #$r SW43Pollywogs 10 SW43P#Pollywogs, obviously. #$r SW43Tadpoles 0 SW43T#Tadpoles, obviously.",
	"Summer.Weekly.4.4": "It might seem counter-intuitive, but you should actually up your salt intake when it's hot out.#$e#Salt helps your body hang on to all that water you should be drinking.",

	"Summer.Weekly.6.1": "You know, I've never taken a Summer vacation.#$b#It's always difficult to justify setting aside the time...",
	"Summer.Weekly.6.2": "Caroline told me once that I'd be less nervous if I replaced my morning coffee with tea.#$e#I don't know if it would really make much of a difference.",
	"Summer.Weekly.6.3": "Summer is definitely my least favorite season.#$e#There's nothing objectively wrong with it, but it's a reminder that the year is half-gone already.",
	"Summer.Weekly.6.4": "Have you seen any butterflies while out and about?#$b#They're very common this time of year.",

	"Summer.Weekly.8.1": "I don't get a lot of free time, so I never know how to spend it when I have some.#$b#It's kind of a silly problem to have.$h",
	"Summer.Weekly.8.2": "I've recently taken an interest in birding.#$e#We often get visited by parrots from the Fern Islands here.$h",
	"Summer.Weekly.8.3": "You're lucky you can spend so much time outside and never get a sunburn.#$e#I feel like I start turning red the second I leave the clinic.",
	"Summer.Weekly.8.4": "Have you ever heard owls out by your farm at night?#$e#The whole time I've been living here, I've never managed to spot one.",

	"Summer.Weekly.10.1": "It's so nice out that I've been considering playing hooky from work.$#e#@, I think you might be a bad influence!#h",
	"Summer.Weekly.10.2": "I got a call from one of my old colleagues the other day. ${He's^She's^They're}$ getting married.#$e#It feels like everyone my age is starting to settle down.",
	"Summer.Weekly.10.3": "Here, @. I thought you might like this. Remember to put it in water so it doesn't wilt in the heat. [421 376 593]$l",
	"Summer.Weekly.10.4": "It's been so difficult to focus on my work lately.#$b#You know, because of the heat.$l",

	"Fall.Weekly.0.1": "This is a particularly good season for foraging.#$e#This might be obvious, but make sure to check that what you find is edible before you eat it.",
	"Fall.Weekly.0.2": "Vinegar is useful in cooking, but it also makes a good natural cleaner.#$b#That is, if you don't mind your kitchen smelling like vinegar.",
	"Fall.Weekly.0.3": "If you start to feel under the weather, don't try to just 'push through'.#$e#It will take you twice as long to get better.",
	"Fall.Weekly.0.4": "Have you started preparing %farm Farm for winter?#$e#Remember to stock up on firewood.",

	"Fall.Weekly.2.1": "In addition to being festive, pumpkins are actually an excellent source of fiber and Vitamin A.",
	"Fall.Weekly.2.2": "PLACEHOLDER 2.2",
	"Fall.Weekly.2.3": "The days will start getting shorter soon. Make sure to plan your farm chores accordingly so you don't get overwhelmed.",
	"Fall.Weekly.2.4": "PLACEHOLDER 2.4",

	"Fall.Weekly.4.1": "It's true that, financially, fall is the best season for the clinic...#$b#Not that I want anyone to get sick!$8",
	"Fall.Weekly.4.2": "Did you know that you can make oil out of sunflower seeds?#$e#I prefer truffle oil for cooking when I can get it, personally.",
	"Fall.Weekly.4.3": "I take patient confidentiality very seriously.#$b#I think that's especially important in a small town, where gossip can spread quickly.",
	"Fall.Weekly.4.4": "If I had to pick a favorite season, I'd probably say Fall.#$e#It's not too hot, not too cold, and there's always an abundance of mushrooms.$h",

	"Fall.Weekly.6.1": "$query MUSEUM_DONATIONS 10 Arch #From what I understand, Stardew Valley is actually an archeological hotspot.#$e#But you'd know all about that, judging by the donations in the museum.$h|From what I understand, Stardew Valley is actually an archeological hotspot.#$e#It makes sense that Gunther decided to settle here.",
	"Fall.Weekly.6.2": "I keep thinking I ought to set up a bird feeder.#$e#I wonder if Robin would be interested in building me one...?",
	"Fall.Weekly.6.3": "I've seen several flocks of birds heading South.#$e#Is it weird to feel a little jealous of them?",
	"Fall.Weekly.6.4": "I imagine decorating for the season is easy for you.#$b#You probably already have a scarecrow up, right?$h",

	"Fall.Weekly.8.1": "When I was younger I used to stay up late reading by the light of my nightlight.#$e#I think that might be part of the reason my eyesight is so bad now...",
	"Fall.Weekly.8.2": "My apartment here is small, but it's still quite a bit larger than the one I had as a student.#$e#When I first moved in it felt downright spacious.",
	"Fall.Weekly.8.3": "I've never really liked Spirit's Eve, but I do like the excuse to roast a bunch of pumpkin seeds.$h",
	"Fall.Weekly.8.4": "I've been reading about the historical background of Spirit's Eve.#$e#Did you know that it used to be more about welcoming the end-of-Summer harvest?#$b#It's kind of like a celebration of farmers, that way!$h",

	"Fall.Weekly.10.1": "If you're feeling chilly, @, you're welcome to borrow my coat.$l",
	"Fall.Weekly.10.2": "Here, @. It's a 'hot drinks' kind of day, I think. Stay warm! [395 614]$h",
	"Fall.Weekly.10.3": "You know what I haven't had in years? A genuine home-made apple cider.#$e#I bet between the two of us we could whip up a blue-ribbon batch.$h",
	"Fall.Weekly.10.4": "PLACEHOLDER 10.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.0.1": "I hope that your farmhouse is properly insulated. It gets very cold here in the valley at night.",
	"Winter.Weekly.0.2": "If you find yourself with a cough, honey works just as well as cough syrup.#$e#Just because I'm a doctor doesn't mean I think home remedies are bunk. If it works, it works!$h",
	"Winter.Weekly.0.3": "If you haven't already invested in heavy-duty boots, now would be the time.",
	"Winter.Weekly.0.4": "PLACEHOLDER 0.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.2.1": "I know that holly berries look tempting, but it's definitely a bad idea to eat them.",
	"Winter.Weekly.2.2": "The valley usually spends all winter covered in snow.#$e#I imagine that might make farming more difficult.",
	"Winter.Weekly.2.3": "PLACEHOLDER 2.3",
	"Winter.Weekly.2.4": "PLACEHOLDER 2.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.4.1": "%revealtaste:Harvey:829 You know, you can actually make a nice tea just by boiling fresh ginger.#$e#You can add cinnamon as well if you'd like a more wintery taste.",
	"Winter.Weekly.4.2": "PLACEHOLDER 4.2",
	"Winter.Weekly.4.3": "PLACEHOLDER 4.3",
	"Winter.Weekly.4.4": "PLACEHOLDER 4.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.6.1": "I once asked Elliot for book recommendations...#$e#I think he and I have slightly different tastes when it comes to literature.",
	"Winter.Weekly.6.2": "$query MUSEUM_DONATIONS 40 Arch Minerals #The museum has really filled up thanks to you.#$e#I guess it makes sense, considering how much digging a farmer must do.$h|It always feels special when there's a new donation to the museum, considering how long it was empty.",
	"Winter.Weekly.6.3": "I worry about Linus in this weather.#$b#I know he can take care of himself, of course. But I still worry.#$e#I hope he'd feel comfortable reaching out if he needed help.",
	"Winter.Weekly.6.4": "I will say, a huge upside to living where I work is that I don't have to walk to work in the snow.",

	"Winter.Weekly.8.1": "PLACEHOLDER 8.1",
	"Winter.Weekly.8.2": "PLACEHOLDER 8.2",
	"Winter.Weekly.8.3": "Gift-giving season is always a little stressful for me.#$e#I worry about getting someone something that they don't want, or that they already have.",
	"Winter.Weekly.8.4": "PLACEHOLDER 8.4",

	"Winter.Weekly.10.1": "Winter always makes me feel a little melancholy...#$b#Less so, this year.$l",
	"Winter.Weekly.10.2": "Here, @. It's a 'hot drinks' kind of day, I think. Stay warm! [395 614]$h",
	"Winter.Weekly.10.3": "This time of year always makes me wish I had a fireplace.#$e#The one in your cabin must be so cozy.$l",
	"Winter.Weekly.10.4": "PLACEHOLDER 10.4",
	
	//Date Specific Dialogue
	
}
